MAINFRAME INFRASTRUCTURE STRATEGY
----------------------------------
The existing z/OS/CICS/DB2 infrastructure is preserved via an EXCI bridge pattern:

  1. PRE-RULE (read path)
     DLISQLUP is called before every ODM ruleset execution.
     It retrieves: application, candidate, driving history, existing licenses,
     and active fee schedule from IBM Db2 for z/OS.
     Results are deserialised into RuleContext for pure in-memory ODM evaluation.

  2. POST-RULE (write path — transactional)
     DLISPAY  — called after payment rules pass:
                INSERT DLIS.PAYMENT + UPDATE DLIS.LICENSE_APPLICATION
     DLISLICS — called after issuance rules pass:
                INSERT DLIS.ISSUED_LICENSE + UPDATE DLIS.LICENSE_APPLICATION

  3. ODM rules are stateless and side-effect-free (pure evaluation only).
     DB2 writes only occur after rules confirm business validity.

  EXCI connectivity:
     Java layer  -->  ExciCicsAdapter.java  -->  CICS TG (TCP/IP)  -->  z/OS CICS region

  Environment variables required:
     CICS_APPLID       VTAM applid of target CICS region (e.g., CICSPROD)
     CICS_USERID       RACF user ID for EXCI invocation (e.g., DLISUSR)
     CICS_COMMAREA_MAX Maximum COMMAREA size in bytes (default: 32767)


DB2 TABLES (IBM Db2 for z/OS — Schema: DLIS)
---------------------------------------------

  Table                   CA Gen Entity            Key Constraints
  ----------------------  -----------------------  ----------------------------
  DLIS.CANDIDATE          CANDIDATE.ENT            PK auto-identity; UQ ID_NUMBER
  DLIS.LICENSE_APPLICATION LICENSE-APPLICATION.ENT FK to CANDIDATE; CHECK all status codes
  DLIS.DRIVING_HISTORY    DRIVING-HISTORY.ENT      FK to CANDIDATE; CHECK incident type
  DLIS.PAYMENT            PAYMENT.ENT              FK to APPLICATION+CANDIDATE; CHECK amount>0
  DLIS.ISSUED_LICENSE     ISSUED-LICENSE.ENT       UQ LICENSE_NUMBER; CHECK expiry>issue
  DLIS.AUTHORITY_USER     AUTHORITY-USER.ENT       UQ USER_CODE; CHECK level in (1,2)
  DLIS.LICENSE_FEE_SCHEDULE LICENSE-FEE-SCHEDULE.ENT CHECK FEE_AMOUNT>0; index on type+date


KEY IMPROVEMENTS OVER CA GEN
------------------------------

  CA Gen                               ODM Architecture
  -----------------------------------  -------------------------------------------
  Rules embedded in generated COBOL    Rules in Decision Center — no regeneration
  No rule change audit trail           Full version history in Decision Center
  Business users cannot edit rules     Browser-based BAL editor in Decision Center
  Rule logic coupled with DB2 I/O      Pure rule evaluation; I/O in CICS adapters
  Changes require full regeneration    Rules hot-deployed via Decision Center
  Testing requires full app rebuild    ODM Rule Unit Test framework for isolation
  Duplicate logic across action blocks Single rule definition shared by all flows


